      {
        "id": "p78-q78",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$|x-1|\\le |x+1|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\ge 0$.",
          "worked": "The midpoint of $-1$ and $1$ is $0$. Points at least as close to $1$ as to $-1$ lie on or to the right of this midpoint. Therefore, $x\\ge 0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p78-q79",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$|2x+1|\\ge |x-3|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p78-q79-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x\\le -4\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x\\ge \\frac23",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p78-q79-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Split into the two outer cases and intersect the conditions within each case.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Split into $2x+1\\ge |x-3|$ or $2x+1\\le -|x-3|$.\n\nFor the first case, both conditions must hold:\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+1&\\ge x-3\\\\x&\\ge -4\\\\2x+1&\\ge -(x-3)\\\\x&\\ge \\frac23\\end{align*}$$\nTheir intersection is $x\\ge \\frac23$.\n\nFor the second case, both conditions must hold:\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+1&\\le x-3\\\\x&\\le -4\\\\2x+1&\\le -(x-3)\\\\x&\\le \\frac23\\end{align*}$$\nTheir intersection is $x\\le -4$.\n\nTherefore, $x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge \\frac23$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 144
      },
      {
        "id": "p78-q80",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$|x+4|<|x-3|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "The midpoint of $-4$ and $3$ is\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{-4+3}{2}&=-\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$\nPoints strictly closer to $-4$ than to $3$ lie to the left of this midpoint. Therefore, $x<-\\frac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p78-q81",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$|3x-2|>|2x+5|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p78-q81-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x<-\\frac35\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x>7",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p78-q81-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Split into the two outer cases; exclude both boundary values.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Split into $3x-2>|2x+5|$ or $3x-2<-|2x+5|$.\n\nFor the first case, both conditions must hold:\n$$\\begin{align*}3x-2&>2x+5\\\\x&>7\\\\3x-2&>-(2x+5)\\\\x&>-\\frac35\\end{align*}$$\nTheir intersection is $x>7$.\n\nFor the second case, both conditions must hold:\n$$\\begin{align*}3x-2&<2x+5\\\\x&<7\\\\3x-2&<-(2x+5)\\\\x&<-\\frac35\\end{align*}$$\nTheir intersection is $x<-\\frac35$.\n\nTherefore, $x<-\\frac35$ or $x>7$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 144
      }
    ]
